WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.868
Ukrainian authorities report

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:04.237
a series of Russian rocket attacks

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.506
hit a residential building

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.708
in the city of Zaporizhzhia overnight.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:09.943
Emergency response

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:11.911
teams rescued nine people,

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.847
including a pregnant woman.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:14.814
The attack killed

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.783
at least two people and rescue

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.785
efforts are ongoing.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.820
Officials are raising concerns

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.455
about the safety of the nearby

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.157
nuclear power plant.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.525
The head of the International

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.828
Atomic Energy Agency says the plant faces

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.698
persistent security risks due to the war.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.801
This Saturday will mark one year since

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:35.702
Russian forces

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.871
seized control of the nuclear site.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.305
And as CNN's Clare

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.441
Sebastian reports, experts are worried

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:43.510
Russia's tight grip on the facility

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.147
could lead to disaster

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.449
A year into its occupation

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.350
of the Parisian

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.718
nuclear power plant,

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:54.254
Russia is making changes.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.255
Satellite images

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.090
showing the dry storage area

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.192
where spent nuclear fuel is kept

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.627
after being cooled

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.762
first in August last year.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.664
Then at the end of February,

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.766
what looks like a wall of structure

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:07.901
has appeared.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.436
Russia's atomic energy company

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.371
Rosatom tells state media

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.173
it's building a shield to protect

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.375
against Ukrainian artillery strikes.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.443
A local Russian backed

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.545
official posted this in December,

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.814
calling it a protective dome.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:21.748
It's only

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.751
doing what was

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:28.521
supposed to impact nuclear safety.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.323
The head of Ukraine's

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.458
atomic energy company

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:31.858
and Erika

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:32.325
Adams

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.726
says it's all part

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.462
of a deteriorating situation.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:36.529
It's a pariah

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.331
that he is powerless to stop.

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:40.433
What is the biggest risk right now

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.969
when it comes to safety in the plant?

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:43.503
Well, yeah,

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:46.039
because those things that we don't know

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.975
what is the fence of the moment

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.111
you can expect.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:51.644
And

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.714
so they continue

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:57.951
shelling on the ground for example,

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:59.552
another atom says Russia,

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.354
which forcibly took over the plant

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.255
last March,

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.690
damaging several buildings

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.691
in the process,

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.059
continues to use it

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.528
as a de facto military base.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:10.230
This video surfaced

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.531
last summer of military

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:13.500
trucks in one of the turbine buildings

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.136
next to a reactor last month.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:17.537
An atom accused Russia

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.072
of bringing hundreds of newly

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.907
mobilized troops to the site

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:23.009
before deploying them to the east.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.210
Rosatom is own press

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.345
service for the power plant,

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.846
denied there's any heavy

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.748
military equipment on site,

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:29.949
but noted that Russia's

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.484
National Guard troops,

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:33.720
Putin's domestic security force,

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.455
are guarding the plant.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.490
I'm very worried about the supplies.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.292
I'm very worried.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.460
And that Atom says

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.027
the plant

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:42.061
has been cut off

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.263
from the electricity grid

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:45.331
five times in total,

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.799
leaving diesel generators

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:47.700
the last line of

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.536
defense before a catastrophe.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:51.771
Fighting has

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:55.241
also come to close

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.111
The IAEA reports shelling into building

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:00.847
housing fresh nuclear fuel in September

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:04.083
and a reactor building in November.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.685
And that atom now estimates

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.020
four and a half thousand

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.054
Ukrainian staff

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:08.488
are left

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.723
at the plant out of 11,000

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:11.858
before the war.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.560
That reduction of the number of people

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.528
is going to have
a significant impact

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.429
on their ability

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.565
to maintain and function sort of systems,

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:19.332
whether or not

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:21.234
that security systems, safety

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.202
systems, radiation

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.937
monitoring, nuclear expert

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.805
Nick Tomkinson says he is working

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.006
with the Ukrainian government

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.575
to try to deploy radiation

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:29.742
mapping systems

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.744
and to Parisa and other nuclear sites.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.680
One of the concerns could be that

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.348
things could go missing

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.984
and bombs are easier, particularly

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:38.818
some of the fuel.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.119
I'm not worried about my.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.254
What I'd be worried about

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.389
was is an active decision

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.024
to do something.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:45.992
Ukraine's nuclear

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:46.593
power company,

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.461
though, is worried about a slow

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:49.829
motion mistake

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:50.730
for maintenance

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.998
leading to the degradation

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.733
of the equipment on the site.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.668
Including the reactors themselves.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.102
Currently,

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.371
all in various states have shut down.

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:01.207
It is bore to the stage, though.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.476
Nobody wants to

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:07.413
if we will be able to operate it.

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:10.183
This is just the start.

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:11.651
The Russian

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:12.252
side says

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.686
strict radiation safety

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:16.055
standards are being observed.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:17.423
Hardly a consolation

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.593
when 20% of Ukraine's electricity supply

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:24.731
remains hostage to this war.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:27.000
Whereas me, there is no let up.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:27.800
The IAEA,

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:28.468
the UN's nuclear

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.369
watchdog, reports

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:32.338
last weekend that the backup power line

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:34.641
connecting the plant to the Ukrainian

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:36.542
electricity grid was severed again.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.810
It was then restored.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.212
The staff there also said

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:42.115
they had around 20 detonations

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:43.883
in the vicinity of the plant.

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.019
This as the IAEA is expressing concern

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.687
that a planned rotation

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:48.721
of staff to that

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:51.557
plant is more than three weeks late.

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:52.759
And I want to point out as well

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:53.960
that Rosatom, Russia's

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:54.527
nuclear energy

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.095
monopoly, continues

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.564
to avoid most Western sanctions,

00:04:58.564 --> 00:04:59.232
even as

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.466
the rest of Russia's energy

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:01.901
industry has been heavily

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.236
sanctioned Rosemary.

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:04.103
Many thanks to Clare

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.438
Sebastian for that report.

